DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The mmooddnneexxtt() system call returns the modid of the next kernel module
     (that is, the one after _m_o_d_i_d) or 0 if _m_o_d_i_d is the last module in the
     list.

     If the _m_o_d_i_d value is 0, then mmooddnneexxtt() will return the modid of the
     first module.  The mmooddffnneexxtt() system call must always be given a valid
     modid.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     The mmooddnneexxtt() system call returns the modid of the next module (see
     _D_E_S_C_R_I_P_T_I_O_N) or 0.  If an error occurs, _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the er‐
     ror.

EERRRROORRSS
     The only error set by mmooddnneexxtt() is ENOENT, which is set when _m_o_d_i_d refers
     to a kernel module that does not exist (is not loaded).

